# Normalise line endings on the way into git.
#
# Without this, a contributor on Windows with core.autocrlf=true commits CRLF,
# and the next contributor on Linux sees every line of the file as changed. The
# diff becomes unreadable and review becomes impossible. Storing LF in the repo
# and letting each checkout use its native endings keeps diffs honest.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.db   binary

# Collapse noise in pull request diffs.
static/v2/**  linguist-vendored
